01:00:58.000 --> 01:00:59.000
he called myths.

cue0035045
01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:01.000
By that I believe he meant

cue0035046
01:01:02.000 --> 01:01:03.000
misperceptions,

cue0035047
01:01:04.000 --> 01:01:05.000
historical misperceptions.

cue0035048
01:01:06.000 --> 01:01:07.000
Whether there are people

cue0035049
01:01:08.000 --> 01:01:09.000
who agree and disagree

cue0035050
01:01:10.000 --> 01:01:11.000
with his comment,

cue0035051
01:01:12.000 --> 01:01:13.000
but the word myth is also

cue0035052
01:01:13.000 --> 01:01:14.000
used in another sense.

cue0035053
01:01:15.000 --> 01:01:16.000
It's used in the sense

cue0035054
01:01:17.000 --> 01:01:18.000
of the stories by which

cue0035055
01:01:19.000 --> 01:01:20.000
we inform our lives

cue0035056
01:01:21.000 --> 01:01:22.000
and shape our consciousness

cue0035057
01:01:23.000 --> 01:01:24.000
and experience the world.

cue0035058
01:01:25.000 --> 01:01:26.000
We need to really

cue0035059
01:01:27.000 --> 01:01:28.000
differentiate those

cue0035060
01:01:29.000 --> 01:01:30.000
two kinds of things,

cue0035061
01:01:31.000 --> 01:01:32.000
because in the examination

cue0035062
01:01:33.000 --> 01:01:34.000
of history,

cue0035063
01:01:35.000 --> 01:01:36.000
we have been told that

cue0035064
01:01:37.000 --> 01:01:38.000
history is a likely story.

cue0035065
01:01:39.000 --> 01:01:40.000
We need to distinguish

cue0035066
01:01:41.000 --> 01:01:42.000
between what happened

cue0035067
01:01:43.000 --> 01:01:44.000
our own structuring

cue0035068
01:01:45.000 --> 01:01:46.000
of the past,

cue0035069
01:01:47.000 --> 01:01:48.000
and finally the stories

cue0035070
01:01:49.000 --> 01:01:50.000
that we need to live by.

cue0035071
01:01:51.000 --> 01:01:52.000
The very question that

cue0035072
01:01:53.000 --> 01:01:54.000
has come up at the end,

cue0035073
01:01:55.000 --> 01:01:56.000
which deals with the

cue0035074
01:01:57.000 --> 01:01:58.000
close interaction possibly

cue0035075
01:01:59.000 --> 01:02:00.000
between Judaism and

cue0035076
01:02:01.000 --> 01:02:02.000
Christianity, may be

cue0035077
01:02:03.000 --> 01:02:04.000
very threatening for

cue0035078
01:02:05.000 --> 01:02:06.000
Jewish communities today.

cue0035079
01:02:07.000 --> 01:02:08.000
That, to quote you,

cue0035080
01:02:09.000 --> 01:02:10.000
doesn't make any difference.

cue0035081
01:02:11.000 --> 01:02:12.000
The question is,

cue0035082
01:02:13.000 --> 01:02:14.000
in the past,

cue0035083
01:02:15.000 --> 01:02:16.000
what really went on?

cue0035084
01:02:17.000 --> 01:02:18.000
I suspect that if we

cue0035085
01:02:19.000 --> 01:02:20.000
look at the past,

cue0035086
01:02:21.000 --> 01:02:22.000
we're going to find,

cue0035087
01:02:23.000 --> 01:02:24.000
as we have experienced

cue0035088
01:02:25.000 --> 01:02:26.000
this morning,

cue0035089
01:02:27.000 --> 01:02:28.000
a very complex picture

cue0035090
01:02:29.000 --> 01:02:30.000
of people,

cue0035091
01:02:31.000 --> 01:02:32.000
Jews and Christians,

cue0035092
01:02:33.000 --> 01:02:34.000
who interacted with

cue0035093
01:02:35.000 --> 01:02:36.000
each other,

cue0035094
01:02:37.000 --> 01:02:38.000
got along very well,

cue0035095
01:02:39.000 --> 01:02:40.000
did business,

cue0035096
01:02:41.000 --> 01:02:42.000
bought and sold,

cue0035097
01:02:43.000 --> 01:02:44.000
based on what they

cue0035098
01:02:45.000 --> 01:02:46.000
considered to be

cue0035099
01:02:47.000 --> 01:02:48.000
sacred scripture.

cue0035100
01:02:49.000 --> 01:02:50.000
The business of history

cue0035101
01:02:51.000 --> 01:02:52.000
is to find the best

cue0035102
